
Conclusion from autocorrelation plot

      Under the null hypothesis of white noise
      (and normality), a 2-sided 95% confidence
      interval for the autocorrelation coefficient

           -0.08      to       0.08

      Under this null hypothesis, only 5
      average) of the computed autocorelations
      should fall outside of this interval

      For this data set, it is observed

           127     out of the      138 (=   92.03%)

      of the computed autocorrelation coefficients fall
      outside of this interval.

Conclusion--based on this autocorrelation
            plot test, there is evidence from
            this data that the hypothesis
            of randomness should be
            rejected.


